<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-Scania 9-mo profit down 25 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Scania 9-mo profit down 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck and bus maker Scania was expected to post a lower profit after financial items for the first nine months of 1996 of 2.65 billion crowns, a Reuters poll of 11 analysts showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>This was a 25 percent fall from the corresponding period a year ago when the company reported a profit after financial items of 3.51 billion crowns.</p>
<p>For the full year 1996 the average of 12 analysts' forecasts showed a profit after financial items of 3.83 billion crowns compared to 4.85 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>Profit per share was expected to be 13.59 crowns.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from Aros, Nordiska, Handelsbanken, Salomon Brothers, Swedbank, Fiba Nordic, Morgan Grenfell, BZW, Danske Bank, Kleinwort Benson, Foreningsbanken and Enskilda.</p>
<p>Scania will release its nine month report on November 7.</p>
